Implement exactly task compose-access-only-live-proxy-mode from:
- docs/product-specs/codex-local-profile-import-workaround.md
- docs/product-specs/codex-local-profile-import-workaround.tasks.json
- docs/exec-plans/active/codex-local-profile-import-workaround.md

You own only apps/codex-proxy/**. Do not edit packages/codex-oauth, docs, task ledgers, execution plans, lockfiles, or git history. You are not alone in the codebase: do not revert other edits and adjust to current state.

Implement app-owned live-mode composition using existing @bundjil/codex-oauth layers:
- compose encrypted KeyValueStore profile storage, cipher/config, Upstash store, Upstash refresh lock, unsupported OAuth client, OAuth service, direct provider, HTTP/fetch, and private OpenAI-compatible proxy;
- retain mock as default and fully working;
- layer selection must happen after decoded CodexProxyConfig, not import-time process.env;
- live calls must use getValidToken only; do not introduce refresh or API-key fallback;
- map missing/expired profile and missing live config to safe 502 with a generic re-import instruction; preserve 401 auth behavior and normal upstream 502 behavior;
- add deterministic tests with mocked Codex fetch / existing package test layers only; no Upstash or network credentials;
- update app README only if necessary to accurately reflect what this task delivers.

Use Effect TS native approaches first. Prefer Data, Schema, Array, Chunk, HashSet, HashMap, Match, Context, Layer, Config, Service, Record, Result, Exit, Bun/Platform Command, and ManagedRuntime over plain TypeScript helpers when code crosses a runtime/service boundary. Reuse canonical contracts/errors. No new DTOs, unsafe casts, JSON.stringify/JSON.parse, process.env, local manual readers/mappers, or trivial wrappers. Keep primary operations flat named Effect.gen with typed errors in .pipe(...).

Run apps/codex-proxy check-types/test/build/smoke-test and bun run verification if practical. Report exact changed files and verification, but do not commit.

